aquinas-third-way.md:1: argue/invalid: C1 (S4): does not follow: when "another3 is possible to be and not to be", "another2 is in existence at time another2", "another3 is in existence at time another" and "another3 is in existence at time another3" are true, and nothing else is true, every premise holds and the conclusion fails; this is a generalization: what holds of the cases named need not hold of every case
